ocket the tests open to the target's port sends AUTH first, and redis-cli and redis-benchmark log in when pointed at it"},{"kind":"rewritten","what":"tests/support/server.tcl: FUNCTION FLUSH before each file","reason":"the harness runs it before every file and stops the file when it is refused; an engine without Functions would fail every file on that one command, which unit/functions and tier 0 measure, so a refusal is tolerated there"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"tests tagged needs:debug, needs:pfdebug, needs:repl, needs:save, needs:reset, needs:config-maxmemory, needs:config-resetstat, needs:other-server, large-memory","reason":"they need a test hook (DEBUG and its kin), a second server or a server setting a test from outside cannot restore"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"CONFIG SET rollback on apply error","reason":"it assumes the test client and the server share a host: it holds a port so that CONFIG SET port must fail, but a server in a container of its own binds the port, moves to it and is unreachable after"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"Interactive CLI: Subscribed mode","reason":"it sends RESET, which logs the connection out, and goes on as if no password were set"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"PUBLISH/PSUBSCRIBE after PUNSUBSCRIBE without arguments","reason":"it publishes on one connection without waiting for the PUNSUBSCRIBE reply on another, so its answer depends on which arrives first; it failed one of four runs on the redis-7.2 reference"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"PUBLISH/SUBSCRIBE after UNSUBSCRIBE without arguments","reason":"the same race as the PSUBSCRIBE test above, with a channel instead of a pattern: it publishes without waiting for the UNSUBSCRIBE reply, and answered ok once where the recording had err"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"BRPOPLPUSH does not affect WATCH while still blocked","reason":"it blocks a deferred client and then watches the target on another connection, so what it asserts depends on the moment the server counts the first client as blocked; it answered err once in three runs on the redis-7.2 reference"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"MONITOR log blocked command only once","reason":"it sends the blocked command on one connection and the info clients polls it waits with on another, then asserts the blocked command is the first line its monitor reads; which one the server feeds the monitor first is a race, and it failed one of three runs on the redis-7.2 reference"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"integration/replication-buffer.tcl (not scored)","reason":"it sizes a replication backlog and reads it back from INFO: the server's buffer accounting, not what a replica receives"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"unit/latency-monitor.tcl (not scored)","reason":"its tests are LATENCY MONITOR's records of the server's own event loop, an ops tool no client sends"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"unit/lazyfree.tcl (not scored)","reason":"it asserts that FLUSHDB ASYNC reclaims memory in the background: an allocator's behavior, measured through the server's memory figures"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"unit/querybuf.tcl (not scored)","reason":"it reads the size of a client's query buffer from CLIENT LIST: the server's own memory management, which no client sees"},{"kind":"left_out","what":"unit/slowlog.tcl (not scored)","reason":"it reads the server's SLOWLOG: an ops tool whose answer is the deployment's thresholds and the host's speed"}],"changes_summary":"14 changes: behavior-equivalent shim, not upstream verbatim: tests/support/redis.tcl: a client socket to the target logs in; rewritten to run here: tests/support/server.tcl: FUNCTION FLUSH before each file; left out: tests tagged needs:debug, needs:pfdebug, needs:repl, needs:save, needs:reset, needs:config-maxmemory, needs:config-resetstat, needs:other-server, large-memory; left out: CONFIG SET rollback on apply error; left out: Interactive CLI: Subscribed mode; left out: PUBLISH/PSUBSCRIBE after PUNSUBSCRIBE without arguments; left out: PUBLISH/SUBSCRIBE after UNSUBSCRIBE with